# Answer key for E3 (e3_joins.sql): shipment joins, one bare SELECT.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE (2026-10-07).
# CLOSED WORLD: every <result> column and every filter is stated. Conventions D-1..D-53.
#
# The row-deciding path is hdr (shipment_header) JOIN shipment_line JOIN customer, plus the
# final WHERE. cs, site, org, wh and plan_vs_ship are reached only through LEFT joins, so
# every predicate inside or on them is a conditional VALUE of what they feed (D-45, D-48,
# D-49), never a filter.

@ 17 the whole statement

# --- inner spine ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
value lgx.shipment_line.shipment_line_id -> <result>.shipment_line_id identity
value lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id -> <result>.shipment_id identity
value crm.customer.customer_name -> <result>.customer_name identity
value lgx.shipment_line.shipped_qty -> <result>.shipped_qty identity

# --- cs: carrier LEFT JOIN (carrier_service NATURAL JOIN transport_mode) USING, WHERE active
value lgx.carrier.carrier_name -> <result>.carrier_name identity
value lgx.carrier_service.service_level -> <result>.service_level identity
value lgx.transport_mode.mode_desc -> <result>.mode_desc identity
value lgx.shipment_line.ship_date, lgx.carrier_service.transit_days -> <result>.expected_delivery derived
note ship_date + COALESCE(transit_days, 0): the COALESCE reads one column (D-19).
value lgx.carrier.active_flag -> <result>.carrier_name, <result>.service_level, <result>.mode_desc, <result>.expected_delivery conditional
note cs's WHERE cr.active_flag cannot remove a result row through the LEFT join: a value of every column cs feeds (D-45).
forbid filter lgx.carrier.active_flag -> <result> | cs is reached only through a LEFT join (D-45)

# --- site: LEFT join with a one-relation ON condition (D-48) -------------------------------
value crm.customer_site.site_code -> <result>.site_code identity
value crm.customer_site.time_zone_name -> <result>.site_code conditional
forbid filter crm.customer_site.time_zone_name -> <result> | on a LEFT join's null side the ON condition removes no row (D-48)

# --- org: LEFT join with a range ON (D-49 on the null side = values, D-48) ------------------
value gold.dim_organization.org_name -> <result>.ship_from_org identity
value gold.dim_organization.organization_start_date, gold.dim_organization.organization_end_date, lgx.shipment_header.created_at -> <result>.ship_from_org conditional
note The key equality org.integration_id = hdr.ship_from_org_id::text stays structural (D-5, D-11).
forbid filter gold.dim_organization.organization_start_date -> <result> | a range condition on a LEFT join's null side decides a value, not a row (D-49, D-48)

# --- wh: organization RIGHT JOIN warehouse ON ... AND o.is_active, itself LEFT joined -------
value lgx.warehouse.warehouse_code -> <result>.warehouse_code identity
value crm.organization.org_name -> <result>.warehouse_org identity
value crm.organization.is_active -> <result>.warehouse_org conditional
forbid value crm.organization.is_active -> <result>.warehouse_code conditional | the RIGHT join keeps every warehouse; is_active only decides whether org_name is filled

# --- plan_vs_ship: FULL JOIN of two aggregates ----------------------------------------------
value lgx.bill_of_material.qty_per -> <result>.planned_qty aggregated
influence lgx.bill_of_material.parent_item_id -> <result>.planned_qty
value lgx.shipment_line.shipped_qty -> <result>.shipped_total aggregated
influence lgx.shipment_line.item_id -> <result>.shipped_total
note The FULL JOIN key and the COALESCE(item_id) join key are structural (D-5).

# --- filters -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
filter lgx.shipment_header.is_deleted -> <result>
filter crm.customer.status -> <result>
note An INNER join's one-relation ON condition removes rows as WHERE would (D-48).
filter lgx.shipment_header.status_code -> <result>
filter lgx.shipment_line.ship_date, lgx.shipment_header.created_at -> <result>
note ln.ship_date >= hdr.created_at::date: a non-equality between two relations, both operands (D-49).
filter lgx.shipment_header.customer_id, crm.contact.customer_id, crm.contact.is_primary -> <result>
note IN (subquery): both match columns and the subquery's WHERE (D-52).
filter lgx.package_event.shipment_id, lgx.shipment_header.shipment_id, lgx.package_event.event_type -> <result>
note NOT EXISTS: both correlation operands and the subquery's own predicate (D-52).
